<article class="env-lemma" id="0222">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0222">Lemma <span data-tag="0222">34.5.4</span>.</a> Let $T$ be an affine scheme. Let $\{ T_ i \to T\} _{i \in I}$ be a smooth covering of $T$. Then there exists a smooth covering $\{ U_ j \to T\} _{j = 1, \ldots , m}$ which is a refinement of $\{ T_ i \to T\} _{i \in I}$ such that each $U_ j$ is an affine scheme, and such that each morphism $U_ j \to T$ is standard smooth, see Morphisms, Definition <a href="/tag/01V5" data-tag="01V5">29.35.1</a>. Moreover, we may choose each $U_ j$ to be open affine in one of the $T_ i$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Omitted, but see Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/00TA" data-tag="00TA">10.137.9</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>